      "writtenOn": "2020-04-07T19:48:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "haha, for sure. That was my first solution. It is actually pretty complicated because of the all, ro, and rw image in the make file\n\nThe overall HAS_TASK_KEYBOARD can be \u0027y\u0027, \u0027ro\u0027, or \u0027rw\u0027 and likewise CONFIG_CMD_KEYBOARD can be \u0027y\u0027, \u0027ro\u0027, and \u0027rw\u0027 in the make file.\n\nThe CONFIG_CMD_KEYBOARD isn\u0027t always rw when HAS_TASK_KEYBOARD is rw, but I think the task should gate if the CMD are present (even if the CONFIG_CMD_KEYBOARD says \u0027y\u0027)\n\n\nWhile typing the explanation up, I thought of a cleaner way to handle everything. Now added a section at the bottom of config.h that undefs CONFIG_CMD_KEYBOARD if HAS_TASK_KEYBOARD isn\u0027t present, then we can use CONFIG_CMD_KEYBOARD directly in the makefile, thoughts?",
